A||||3||86SE||Battery Drained,........... runs like crap........||||8||
Z||000000||86SE||02-13-2000||01:07 AM||||Ok last night I went to the basketball game, got home switched off my headlights but the right one dident go down.  It was cold outside so I dident want to open the hood and tap on the top of the motor for it to go down so I figured it wasent hurting anything so i left it up all night.  Went to start it at noon when I woke up and the battery was completely dead!!  Hooked it up to the ol Ford pickup and let it run for 5 minutes to get enough juice to turn the Fiero V-6 motor over.  Turned the key and it turned over rather fast and acted like it wanted to start, like it got a spark, fired once and stalled, then I tried it again and I had to give it half throttle before it would start!!  It started and ran like shi*, i had to keep the throttle open half way to keep the engine at 1500 RPM!!  After about a minute and A LOT of white smoke the engine ran just fine.<P>What would cause something like that to happen??||||reg||8
Z||000001||Patrick||02-13-2000||02:43 AM||||<BR>With a dead battery, your ECM probably lost all its settings. The same thing happens when you disconnect your battery to reset the trouble codes after you've done some work to the engine. You have to drive the car for something like ten minutes at 30 MPH for the ECM to set itself up again.||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||02-13-2000||09:57 AM||||You probably bought that battery, didn't you?  Patrick makes his own.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DRH||02-14-2000||01:27 PM||||An extremely low battery can make a computer controlled car do very strange things. If it's OK after the battery gets fully charged I wouldn't worry about it.<BR>||||reg||1
